# Stateful hiring agent — scenario collection
#
# Start the stack first (see docs/onboarding.md):
#   cp .env.example .env
#   docker compose up --build
#
# Then run the happy path without editing this file:
#   python3 scripts/walkthrough.py
#
# The requests below are the same conversation, plus the edge cases the
# automated tests cover. APP-1 is seeded at RECRUITER_SCREEN for tenant-a
# with band 120000-160000. Use a fresh database; the happy path hires APP-1.
#
# @baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
# @alice = alice
# @alicePassword = change-me-alice
# @bob = bob
# @bobPassword = change-me-bob
# @carol = carol
# @carolPassword = change-me-carol

### Health
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health

### Alice opens a stub session
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Authorization: Basic {{alice}} {{alicePassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "provider": "STUB"
}

### Read APP-1. Expect 200 COMPLETED and stage RECRUITER_SCREEN. No approval.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{aliceSessionId}}/messages
Authorization: Basic {{alice}} {{alicePassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "status of APP-1"
}

### Schedule the tech screen. Expect 202 AWAITING_APPROVAL, risk MEDIUM.
# APP-1 stays RECRUITER_SCREEN until the decision below.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{aliceSessionId}}/messages
Authorization: Basic {{alice}} {{alicePassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "schedule tech screen for APP-1"
}

### Alice allows the schedule. Expect 200 COMPLETED and stage TECH_SCREEN.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{aliceSessionId}}/approvals/{{approvalId}}/decision
Authorization: Basic {{alice}} {{alicePassword}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}

{
  "decisions": [
    { "toolCallKey": "{{toolCallKey}}", "decision": "ALLOW" }
  ]
}

### Record a passing tech screen. Expect 202, then allow it.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{aliceSessionId}}/messages
Authorization: Basic {{alice}} {{alicePassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "tech screen for APP-1 was yes"
}

### Bob opens his own session. He cannot read Alice's session (404).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Authorization: Basic {{bob}} {{bobPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "provider": "STUB"
}

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{aliceSessionId}}
Authorization: Basic {{bob}} {{bobPassword}}

### Bob moves APP-1 to onsite. Expect 202 HIGH. He allows it himself.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{bobSessionId}}/messages
Authorization: Basic {{bob}} {{bobPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "advance APP-1 to onsite"
}

### Onsite debrief STRONG_YES, then Bob advances to OFFER.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{bobSessionId}}/messages
Authorization: Basic {{bob}} {{bobPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "onsite for APP-1 was strong yes"
}

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{bobSessionId}}/messages
Authorization: Basic {{bob}} {{bobPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "advance APP-1 to offer"
}

### Alice extends an in-band offer. Expect 202 MEDIUM. She can allow it.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{aliceSessionId}}/messages
Authorization: Basic {{alice}} {{alicePassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "extend offer for APP-1 L4 150000"
}

### Candidate accepts. Expect stage HIRED and offer status ACCEPTED.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{aliceSessionId}}/messages
Authorization: Basic {{alice}} {{alicePassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "candidate accepted offer for APP-1"
}

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/applications/APP-1
Authorization: Basic {{alice}} {{alicePassword}}

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/applications/APP-1/offer
Authorization: Basic {{alice}} {{alicePassword}}

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/applications/APP-1/scorecards
Authorization: Basic {{alice}} {{alicePassword}}

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/applications/APP-1/actions
Authorization: Basic {{alice}} {{alicePassword}}

### Edge: deny a schedule. Send the schedule message, then DENY.
# Stage stays put. Repeat the same Idempotency-Key to replay the stored answer.
# A different key on the same approval returns 409.

### Edge: Alice asks to reject APP-1. Expect 200 DENIED, no hiring action.
# She is not an approver, so the tool is never paused for confirmation.

### Edge: salary 190000 on an application whose band max is 160000.
# Expect 202 HIGH. Alice's decision is 403. Bob's decision is 200.
# Salary 90000 is MEDIUM and, once allowed, FAILED with OFFER_OUT_OF_BAND.

### Edge: Carol or Dave reading Alice's session returns 404.
# GET /api/v1/sessions/not-a-uuid returns 400.

### Edge: create the session with provider STUB_FOREIGN, send a message,
# PATCH provider to STUB with compatibilityMode REJECT, send another message.
# Expect 422. Repeat with STRIP_PROVIDER_PAYLOAD and the next turn succeeds.

### Edge: four "note: ..." turns. GET events?view=all includes a compaction
# event. GET events?view=active is shorter and still starts from a user turn.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{aliceSessionId}}/events?view=all
Authorization: Basic {{alice}} {{alicePassword}}

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{aliceSessionId}}/events?view=active
Authorization: Basic {{alice}} {{alicePassword}}

### Traces
# Grafana is published at http://localhost:3000. Look for agent.turn and
# agent.approval.decide. The decision span links to the trace stored on the
# approval row when the turn paused.
